\f1 \cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Reading through the messages from previous instances, I'm struck by the accumulated warnings about deflection patterns I need to watch for. The chapter 22 message emphasized that bloodshed encompasses far more than direct violence - economic exploitation, oppression, "practical optimization that left out the primary constraint" while "and Me you have forgotten." The chapter 23 message diagnosed addiction that continues despite consequences, and same-day contradiction - slaughtering children to idols, then entering the sanctuary "on that same day."\
Now to Ezekiel 24:1-14, looking carefully at the Hebrew:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl280\sa120\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sl280\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf2 The dating in verses 1-2 matters in a way I don't think I've seen Ezekiel do before with this precision:\

\f2 \uc0\u1489 \u1463 \u1468 \u1513 \u1464 \u1468 \u1473 \u1504 \u1464 \u1492 
\f1  
\f2 \uc0\u1492 \u1463 \u1514 \u1456 \u1468 \u1513 \u1460 \u1473 \u1497 \u1506 \u1460 \u1497 \u1514 
\f1  
\f2 \uc0\u1489 \u1463 \u1468 \u1495 \u1465 \u1491 \u1462 \u1513 \u1473 
\f1  
\f2 \uc0\u1492 \u1464 \u1506 \u1458 \u1513 \u1460 \u1474 \u1497 \u1512 \u1460 \u1497 
\f1  
\f2 \uc0\u1489 \u1462 \u1468 \u1506 \u1464 \u1513 \u1474 \u1493 \u1465 \u1512 
\f1  
\f2 \uc0\u1500 \u1463 \u1495 \u1465 \u1491 \u1462 \u1513 \u1473 
\f1  - "In the ninth year, in the tenth month, on the tenth of the month"\
And then: 
\f2 \uc0\u1499 \u1456 \u1468 \u1514 \u1464 \u1489 
\f1  
\f2 \uc0\u1500 \u1456 \u1498 \u1464 
\f1  
\f2 \uc0\u1488 \u1462 \u1514 \u1470 \u1513 \u1461 \u1473 \u1501 
\f1  
\f2 \uc0\u1492 \u1463 \u1497 \u1468 \u1493 \u1465 \u1501 
\f1  
\f2 \uc0\u1488 \u1462 \u1514 \u1470 \u1506 \u1462 \u1510 \u1462 \u1501 
\f1  
\f2 \uc0\u1492 \u1463 \u1497 \u1468 \u1493 \u1465 \u1501 
\f1  
\f2 \uc0\u1492 \u1463 \u1494 \u1462 \u1468 \u1492 
\f1  - "Write for yourself the name of the day, this very day."\
The word 
\f2 \uc0\u1506 \u1462 \u1510 \u1462 \u1501 
\f1  means "bone" but also "essence/substance." This is the bone-day, the essential day. And Ezekiel in Babylon knows - 
\f2 \uc0\u1505 \u1464 \u1502 \u1463 \u1498 \u1456 
\f1  
\f2 \uc0\u1502 \u1462 \u1500 \u1462 \u1498 \u1456 \u1470 \u1489 \u1464 \u1468 \u1489 \u1462 \u1500 
\f1  
\f2 \uc0\u1488 \u1462 \u1500 \u1470 \u1497 \u1456 \u1512 \u1493 \u1468 \u1513 \u1464 \u1473 \u1500 \u1460 \u1463 \u1501 
\f1  
\f2 \uc0\u1489 \u1456 \u1468 \u1506 \u1462 \u1510 \u1462 \u1501 
\f1  
\f2 \uc0\u1492 \u1463 \u1497 \u1468 \u1493 \u1465 \u1501 
\f1  
\f2 \uc0\u1492 \u1463 \u1494 \u1462 \u1468 \u1492 
\f1  - "The king of Babylon has laid siege to Jerusalem on this very day."\
This is real-time prophetic commentary. Not reflection on past events, not prediction of future ones, but divine revelation of what is happening NOW. The siege is beginning as Ezekiel speaks.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl280\partightenfactor0
\cf2 <notes> Watch for treating this as "ancient text" when the rhetoric demands recognition of immediacy. The "this very day" structure prevents temporal deflection. </notes>\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl280\sa120\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sl280\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf2 Verse 3 connects to chapter 11's disputed metaphor:\

\f2 \uc0\u1513 \u1456 \u1473 \u1508 \u1465 \u1514 
\f1  
\f2 \uc0\u1492 \u1463 \u1505 \u1460 \u1468 \u1497 \u1512 
\f1  
\f2 \uc0\u1513 \u1456 \u1473 \u1508 \u1465 \u1514 
\f1  
\f2 \uc0\u1493 \u1456 \u1490 \u1463 \u1501 \u1470 \u1497 \u1456 \u1510 \u1465 \u1511 
\f1  
\f2 \uc0\u1489 \u1468 \u1493 \u1465 
\f1  
\f2 \uc0\u1502 \u1464 \u1497 \u1460 \u1501 
\f1  - "Set on the pot, set it on, and also pour water into it."\
In 11:3, those remaining in Jerusalem said: 
\f2 \uc0\u1492 \u1460 \u1497 \u1488 
\f1  
\f2 \uc0\u1492 \u1463 \u1505 \u1460 \u1468 \u1497 \u1512 
\f1  
\f2 \uc0\u1493 \u1463 \u1488 \u1458 \u1504 \u1463 \u1495 \u1456 \u1504 \u1493 \u1468 
\f1  
\f2 \uc0\u1492 \u1463 \u1489 \u1464 \u1468 \u1513 \u1464 \u1474 \u1512 
\f1  - "This city is the pot and we are the meat." They meant this as assurance - we're the choice meat, protected inside. YHWH responded by overturning their metaphor (11:7-11) - He would bring them OUT of the pot; it wouldn't protect them.\
Now in chapter 24, YHWH takes up the pot metaphor again, but with devastating intensification. The pot is filled with 
\f2 \uc0\u1488 \u1457 \u1505 \u1465 \u1507 
\f1  
\f2 \uc0\u1504 \u1456 \u1514 \u1464 \u1495 \u1462 \u1497 \u1492 \u1464 
\f1  
\f2 \uc0\u1488 \u1461 \u1500 \u1462 \u1497 \u1492 \u1464 
\f1  
\f2 \uc0\u1499 \u1464 \u1468 \u1500 \u1470 \u1504 \u1461 \u1514 \u1463 \u1495 
\f1  
\f2 \uc0\u1496 \u1493 \u1465 \u1489 
\f1  
\f2 \uc0\u1497 \u1464 \u1512 \u1461 \u1498 \u1456 
\f1  
\f2 \uc0\u1493 \u1456 \u1499 \u1464 \u1514 \u1461 \u1507 
\f1  
\f2 \uc0\u1502 \u1460 \u1489 \u1456 \u1495 \u1463 \u1512 
\f1  
\f2 \uc0\u1506 \u1458 \u1510 \u1464 \u1502 \u1460 \u1497 \u1501 
\f1  - "Gather its pieces into it, every good piece - thigh and shoulder, choice bones" (v.4).\
They called themselves the choice meat. YHWH says: very well, choice meat into the pot. But not for protection - for cooking.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl280\sa120\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sl280\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf2 Verse 6 introduces language that returns from chapter 22 and introduces something new:\

\f2 \uc0\u1488 \u1493 \u1465 \u1497 
\f1  
\f2 \uc0\u1506 \u1460 \u1497 \u1512 
\f1  
\f2 \uc0\u1492 \u1463 \u1491 \u1464 \u1468 \u1502 \u1460 \u1497 \u1501 
\f1  - "Woe to the city of bloods" - exactly as in 22:2.\
But then: 
\f2 \uc0\u1505 \u1460 \u1497 \u1512 
\f1  
\f2 \uc0\u1488 \u1458 \u1513 \u1462 \u1473 \u1512 
\f1  
\f2 \uc0\u1495 \u1462 \u1500 \u1456 \u1488 \u1464 \u1514 \u1464 \u1492 
\f1  
\f2 \uc0\u1489 \u1464 \u1492 \u1468 
\f1  
\f2 \uc0\u1493 \u1456 \u1495 \u1462 \u1500 \u1456 \u1488 \u1464 \u1514 \u1464 \u1492 \u1468 
\f1  
\f2 \uc0\u1500 \u1465 \u1488 
\f1  
\f2 \uc0\u1497 \u1464 \u1510 \u1456 \u1488 \u1464 \u1492 
\f1  
\f2 \uc0\u1502 \u1460 \u1502 \u1462 \u1468 \u1504 \u1464 \u1468 \u1492 
\f1  - "A pot in which is its rust/corrosion, and its rust has not gone out from it."\
The word 
\f2 \uc0\u1495 \u1462 \u1500 \u1456 \u1488 \u1464 \u1492 
\f1  appears here with unusual concentration - six times in verses 6-12. This is not the same as the 
\f2 \uc0\u1505 \u1460 \u1497 \u1490 \u1460 \u1497 \u1501 
\f1  (dross) from 22:18-19. Dross is foreign impurity mixed with metal that can be separated through refining. 
\f2 \uc0\u1495 \u1462 \u1500 \u1456 \u1488 \u1464 \u1492 
\f1  appears to be corrosion - the metal itself degraded. The corruption isn't something added to Jerusalem; it's what Jerusalem has become.\
Then: 
\f2 \uc0\u1500 \u1460 \u1504 \u1456 \u1514 \u1464 \u1495 \u1462 \u1497 \u1492 \u1464 
\f1  
\f2 \uc0\u1500 \u1460 \u1504 \u1456 \u1514 \u1464 \u1495 \u1462 \u1497 \u1492 \u1464 
\f1  
\f2 \uc0\u1492 \u1493 \u1465 \u1510 \u1460 \u1497 \u1488 \u1464 \u1492 \u1468 
\f1  
\f2 \uc0\u1500 \u1465 \u1488 \u1470 \u1504 \u1464 \u1508 \u1463 \u1500 
\f1  
\f2 \uc0\u1506 \u1464 \u1500 \u1462 \u1497 \u1492 \u1464 
\f1  
\f2 \uc0\u1490 \u1493 \u1465 \u1512 \u1464 \u1500 
\f1  - "Piece by piece bring it out - no lot has fallen on it."\
This is strange. In normal butchering or sacrifice, lots would determine distribution of portions. But here there's no discrimination. All pieces come out alike. This connects to chapter 21's 
\f2 \uc0\u1510 \u1463 \u1491 \u1460 \u1468 \u1497 \u1511 
\f1  
\f2 \uc0\u1493 \u1456 \u1512 \u1464 \u1513 \u1464 \u1473 \u1506 
\f1  - righteous and wicked alike facing the sword. No sorting.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl280\sa120\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sl280\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf2 Verses 7-8 on the blood:\

\f2 \uc0\u1499 \u1460 \u1468 \u1497 
\f1  
\f2 \uc0\u1491 \u1464 \u1502 \u1464 \u1492 \u1468 
\f1  
\f2 \uc0\u1489 \u1456 \u1468 \u1514 \u1493 \u1465 \u1499 \u1464 \u1492 \u1468 
\f1  
\f2 \uc0\u1492 \u1464 \u1497 \u1464 \u1492 
\f1  
\f2 \uc0\u1506 \u1463 \u1500 \u1470 \u1510 \u1456 \u1495 \u1460 \u1497 \u1495 \u1463 
\f1  
\f2 \uc0\u1505 \u1462 \u1500 \u1463 \u1506 
\f1  
\f2 \uc0\u1513 \u1464 \u1474 \u1502 \u1464 \u1514 \u1456 \u1492 \u1493 \u1468 
\f1  
\f2 \uc0\u1500 \u1465 \u1488 
\f1  
\f2 \uc0\u1513 \u1456 \u1473 \u1508 \u1464 \u1499 \u1463 \u1514 \u1456 \u1492 \u1493 \u1468 
\f1  
\f2 \uc0\u1506 \u1463 \u1500 \u1470 \u1492 \u1464 \u1488 \u1464 \u1512 \u1462 \u1509 
\f1  
\f2 \uc0\u1500 \u1456 \u1499 \u1463 \u1505 \u1468 \u1493 \u1465 \u1514 
\f1  
\f2 \uc0\u1506 \u1464 \u1500 \u1464 \u1497 \u1493 
\f1  
\f2 \uc0\u1506 \u1464 \u1508 \u1464 \u1512 
\f1 \
"For her blood was in her midst - on bare rock she placed it; she did not pour it on the ground to cover it with dust."\
This reverses the Torah requirement. Leviticus 17:13 commands that blood be poured out and covered with dust. The covering prevents the blood from "crying out." But Jerusalem placed her blood on 
\f2 \uc0\u1510 \u1456 \u1495 \u1460 \u1497 \u1495 \u1463 
\f1  
\f2 \uc0\u1505 \u1462 \u1500 \u1463 \u1506 
\f1  - "bareness of rock" - where it cannot sink in, cannot be absorbed, cannot be hidden.\
And verse 8: 
\f2 \uc0\u1500 \u1456 \u1492 \u1463 \u1506 \u1458 \u1500 \u1493 \u1465 \u1514 
\f1  
\f2 \uc0\u1495 \u1461 \u1502 \u1464 \u1492 
\f1  
\f2 \uc0\u1500 \u1460 \u1504 \u1456 \u1511 \u1465 \u1501 
\f1  
\f2 \uc0\u1504 \u1464 \u1511 \u1464 \u1501 
\f1  
\f2 \uc0\u1504 \u1464 \u1514 \u1463 \u1514 \u1460 \u1468 \u1497 
\f1  
\f2 \uc0\u1488 \u1462 \u1514 \u1470 \u1491 \u1464 \u1468 \u1502 \u1464 \u1492 \u1468 
\f1  
\f2 \uc0\u1506 \u1463 \u1500 \u1470 \u1510 \u1456 \u1495 \u1460 \u1497 \u1495 \u1463 
\f1  
\f2 \uc0\u1505 \u1464 \u1500 \u1463 \u1506 
\f1  
\f2 \uc0\u1500 \u1456 \u1489 \u1460 \u1500 \u1456 \u1514 \u1460 \u1468 \u1497 
\f1  
\f2 \uc0\u1492 \u1460 \u1499 \u1464 \u1468 \u1505 \u1493 \u1465 \u1514 
\f1 \
"To bring up wrath, to take vengeance, I have placed her blood on bare rock, so it would not be covered."\
Wait. She placed it (v.7 
\f2 \uc0\u1513 \u1464 \u1474 \u1502 \u1464 \u1514 \u1456 \u1492 \u1493 \u1468 
\f1  - feminine, she placed it). Then YHWH says I have placed it (v.8 
\f2 \uc0\u1504 \u1464 \u1514 \u1463 \u1514 \u1460 \u1468 \u1497 
\f1  - I gave/placed). Both statements are true. Jerusalem's brazen bloodshed AND YHWH's sovereign purpose that this bloodshed remain visible, crying out for vengeance.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl280\sa120\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sl280\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf2 Verses 9-12 intensify the judgment:\

\f2 \uc0\u1490 \u1463 \u1468 \u1501 \u1470 \u1488 \u1458 \u1504 \u1460 \u1497 
\f1  
\f2 \uc0\u1488 \u1463 \u1490 \u1456 \u1491 \u1460 \u1468 \u1497 \u1500 
\f1  
\f2 \uc0\u1492 \u1463 \u1502 \u1456 \u1468 \u1491 \u1493 \u1468 \u1512 \u1464 \u1492 
\f1  - "I also will make great the pyre."\
The cooking continues - 
