Your argument for the modal reading ("I would have cleansed you but you would not be cleansed") makes sense given the context. The prophets, the good kings, the Torah itself - all offered cleansing. The opportunity existed repeatedly.\
The rhetorical function: this prevents any claim that judgment is arbitrary or that they weren't given chances. The fire coming now isn't YHWH's first choice but His final resort after cleansing was refused.\
But more than that - the reference to 
\f2 \uc0\u1494 \u1460 \u1502 \u1464 \u1468 \u1492 
