\b \cf2 On why this is called a parable (
\f3 \uc0\u1502 \u1464 \u1513 \u1464 \u1473 \u1500 
\f1 ):
\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sl280\partightenfactor0
\cf2 <notes> This question feels important. I'm tempted to give a quick answer about parables being illustrative stories. But the user points to chapter 11's dispute over a saying. Let me think about what 
\f2 \uc0\u1502 \u1464 \u1513 \u1464 \u1473 \u1500 
\f1  means in this context. </notes>\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl280\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf2 In chapter 11, the people had a saying: "This city is the pot and we are the meat." They meant it as comfort - we're the choice portions, protected within the walls.\
A 
\f2 \uc0\u1502 \u1464 \u1513 \u1464 \u1473 \u1500 
\f1  can mean proverb, saying, or parable - something that encapsulates wisdom or truth in memorable form. The people's saying in chapter 11 was their 
\f2 \uc0\u1502 \u1464 \u1513 \u1464 \u1473 \u1500 
\f1  - their way of understanding their situation.\
When Ezekiel is told to speak a 
\f2 \uc0\u1502 \u1464 \u1513 \u1464 \u1473 \u1500 
\f1  to the rebellious house, he's being told to give them a counter-saying. They have their 
\f2 \uc0\u1502 \u1464 \u1513 \u1464 \u1473 \u1500 
\f1  about the pot; YHWH has His. And YHWH's 
\f2 \uc0\u1502 \u1464 \u1513 \u1464 \u1473 \u1500 
\f1  uses their own imagery against them.\
This is the rhetorical function: Ezekiel takes the very metaphor they've used for false comfort and fills it with true content. You say you're the meat in the pot? Yes - corrupted meat being cooked. You say the pot protects you? Yes - a corrupted pot that itself must be destroyed.\
The 
\f2 \uc0\u1502 \u1464 \u1513 \u1464 \u1473 \u1500 
\f1  works by taking their framework and showing what it actually means. They can't escape into different imagery because YHWH is using their imagery. They're trapped within their own metaphor, now filled with judgment instead of comfort.\
This connects to the chapter 19 analysis of forcing the audience to analyze rather than deflect. The parable form, using their own saying, makes deflection impossible. They must either abandon their 
\f2 \uc0\u1502 \u1464 \u1513 \u1464 \u1473 \u1500 
\f1  or hear what it actually means.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl280\sa120\partightenfactor0
