\f2 \uc0\u1488 \u1462 \u1514 \u1470 \u1502 \u1460 \u1511 \u1456 \u1491 \u1464 \u1468 \u1513 \u1460 \u1473 \u1497 
\f1  - "Behold I am PROFANING my sanctuary."\

\f2 \uc0\u1502 \u1456 \u1495 \u1463 \u1500 \u1461 \u1468 \u1500 
\f1  - from 
\f2 \uc0\u1495 \u1500 \u1500 
\f1 , to profane, to make common, to desecrate. YHWH Himself profanes His own sanctuary.\
This is... extraordinary. The sanctuary is holy because YHWH made it holy, because His presence dwelt there. For YHWH to profane it means He is removing His own holiness from it. The temple becomes just a building.\
But wait - chapter 11 already showed the glory departing. The profaning isn't Babylon's violence but YHWH's withdrawal. By the time Babylon destroys the building, YHWH has already made it profane - just stones.\
What was their hope in? The temple as 
\f2 \uc0\u1514 \u1460 \u1468 \u1508 \u1456 \u1488 \u1462 \u1512 \u1462 \u1514 
\f1  (glory), as 
\f2 \uc0\u1502 \u1464 \u1506 \u1493 \u1465 \u1494 
\f1  (stronghold), as what their soul lifted up to. They trusted in the building, the institution, the visible sign of divine presence.\
YHWH takes that. Not by allowing enemies to destroy what's holy, but by removing the holiness first. The enemies destroy what's already profane.\
The hope... is that this exposure is truthful? They were trusting in something that had become corrupted (the pot with its 
\f2 \uc0\u1495 \u1462 \u1500 \u1456 \u1488 \u1464 \u1492 
\f1 ). YHWH removes the false hope so they can no longer hide in it.\
And Ezekiel's prohibited mourning: they cannot mourn like innocent bereaved because 
\f2 \uc0\u1493 \u1468 \u1504 \u1456 \u1502 \u1463 \u1511 \u1465 \u1468 \u1514 \u1462 \u1501 
\f1  
\f2 \uc0\u1489 \u1463 \u1468 \u1506 \u1458 \u1493 \u1465 \u1504 \u1465 \u1514 \u1461 \u1497 \u1499 \u1462 \u1501 
\f1  - "you will rot away in your iniquities." The loss reveals their guilt. Normal mourning would treat them as victims. But they're not victims - they're participants in what brought this judgment.\
The recognition formula: 
\f2 \uc0\u1493 \u1456 \u1497 \u1464 \u1491 \u1456 \u1506 \u1493 \u1468 
\f1  
\f2 \uc0\u1499 \u1460 \u1468 \u1497 \u1470 \u1488 \u1458 \u1504 \u1460 \u1497 
\f1  
\f2 \uc0\u1497 \u1456 \u1492 \u1465 \u1493 \u1464 \u1492 
\f1  - "they will know that I am YHWH."\
They will KNOW. Not through the temple they trusted in, which has been profaned. Not through the comforting lies of false prophets. Not through their defensive narratives. They will know through the very stripping away of everything they wrongly trusted.\
The hope is that the purpose of all this is recognition - not punishment for its own sake, but that they would finally know who YHWH is. The fury continues until recognition comes. But recognition IS the goal.\
And Ezekiel's mouth being opened when the fugitive comes - he has been silent, acting out judgment without words. When the news arrives, he speaks again. Perhaps because now, finally, they might listen? Now that everything false has been stripped away?\
