\cf2 Ezekiel 24 places the audience at step 4 - rotting in iniquity. The prohibition on mourning prevents them from processing the loss as innocent suffering (which would block confession). Ezekiel's sign shows them what they will experience. And then his mouth is opened.\
The opening of Ezekiel's mouth when the news comes might correspond to the possibility of step 5 - confession. Up until now, they couldn't hear reproof because they were defending their false hopes. Now there's nothing to defend. Now Ezekiel can speak to them as 
\f2 \uc0\u1502 \u1493 \u1465 \u1499 \u1460 \u1497 \u1495 \u1463 
\f1 , calling them to confession.\
The hope is that the stripping away opens a path that was blocked before. They couldn't confess while trusting in the temple. They couldn't be humbled while their hearts were defended. They couldn't hear reproof while they had something to be rebellious about.\
Now they have nothing. And "nothing" is the place where Leviticus 26 says confession can begin.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl280\sa120\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sl280\sa240\partightenfactor0
