\f1  - "The hand of YHWH was upon me in the evening before the fugitive came, and He opened my mouth before he came to me in the morning."\
YHWH opens Ezekiel's mouth BEFORE the fugitive arrives. The opening precedes the news. When the fugitive arrives, Ezekiel is already able to speak.\
And what comes after chapter 33? The shepherds oracle (34), the mountains oracle (35-36), the valley of dry bones (37), the Gog oracles (38-39), the temple vision (40-48).\
The opened mouth brings oracles of restoration, not just continued judgment. Shepherds will be replaced by the one shepherd. The land will be restored. The dry bones will live. A new temple will be built with YHWH's presence returning.\
The hope embedded in chapter 24 isn't visible yet, but it's structurally present. The mouth that opens is the mouth that will speak restoration. The rotting in iniquity is the place where confession can begin. The stripped-away temple is the precondition for the future temple where YHWH's glory returns.\
