\b \cf2 On the iron wall and Ezekiel's face:
\b0 \
In chapter 4:3, Ezekiel sets up an iron wall (
\f2 \uc0\u1502 \u1463 \u1495 \u1458 \u1489 \u1463 \u1514 
\f1  
\f2 \uc0\u1489 \u1463 \u1468 \u1512 \u1456 \u1494 \u1462 \u1500 
\f1 ) between himself and the model of besieged Jerusalem: 
\f2 \uc0\u1493 \u1456 \u1504 \u1464 \u1514 \u1463 \u1514 \u1464 \u1468 \u1492 
\f1  
\f2 \uc0\u1488 \u1465 \u1514 \u1464 \u1492 \u1468 
\f1  
\f2 \uc0\u1511 \u1460 \u1497 \u1512 
\f1  
\f2 \uc0\u1489 \u1463 \u1468 \u1512 \u1456 \u1494 \u1462 \u1500 
\f1  
\f2 \uc0\u1489 \u1461 \u1468 \u1497 \u1504 \u1456 \u1498 \u1464 
\f1  
\f2 \uc0\u1493 \u1468 \u1489 \u1461 \u1497 \u1503 
\f1  
\f2 \uc0\u1492 \u1464 \u1506 \u1460 \u1497 \u1512 
\f1  - "and you shall set it as an iron wall between you and the city."\
Then: 
\f2 \uc0\u1493 \u1463 \u1492 \u1458 \u1499 \u1460 \u1497 \u1504 \u1465 \u1514 \u1464 \u1492 
\f1  
\f2 \uc0\u1488 \u1462 \u1514 \u1470 \u1508 \u1464 \u1468 \u1504 \u1462 \u1497 \u1498 \u1464 
\f1  
\f2 \uc0\u1488 \u1461 \u1500 \u1462 \u1497 \u1492 \u1464 
\f1  - "and you shall set your face against it."\
Ezekiel represents YHWH in this sign. The iron wall is the barrier YHWH has placed between Himself and Jerusalem. The set face is YHWH's determined opposition. And Ezekiel is restricted to speaking only judgment oracles - no reproof, no call to repentance that might be heeded.\
The iron wall means no intercession can pass through. Ezekiel faces Jerusalem but cannot reach it. YHWH faces Jerusalem but will not relent.\
Now in chapter 24, the mouth is opened. The restriction ends. The iron wall... is the iron wall removed?\
If Ezekiel as sign represented YHWH's face set against Jerusalem, and now Ezekiel's mouth is opened to speak freely, does this mean YHWH's posture toward the people changes? Not that the judgment is averted - Jerusalem falls - but that after the fall, the barrier comes down?\
The sign in chapter 4: YHWH against the city, no reproof permitted. The sign in chapter 24: mouth opened, able to speak.\
The transition between these two states happens when the city falls. The very thing the iron wall prevented - communication that isn't just judgment - becomes possible when judgment is complete.\
