\f1  - "you will know that I am YHWH."\
YHWH gives up His dwelling place among them so that they will finally know Him. The temple had become an obstacle to knowing - they trusted in the building rather than the God whose presence made it holy. The sanctuary had to go so that YHWH Himself could be known.\
And Ezekiel gives up his wife so that this can be signified. The prophet's personal loss serves the same purpose as YHWH's profaning of the sanctuary - both create conditions for recognition that wasn't possible while those precious things remained.\
