\cf2 What this means for reading the transition:\
Chapters 1-24 end not with resolution but with the creation of conditions. The loss has happened. The mourning is prohibited. The people will rot in their iniquities. Ezekiel's mouth will open.\
What comes next - the oracles against nations (25-32), then the restoration oracles (33-48) - flows from these conditions. The word that judged will restore. The mouth that was closed will speak life. The bones that rotted will rise.\
But none of that is visible in chapter 24. Chapter 24 creates the space where those words can be spoken and heard. The path is made real by the word, but the path begins in the darkness of unmourned loss, in the rotting that precedes confession, in the stripped-away condition where nothing remains but YHWH and what YHWH speaks.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl280\sa120\partightenfactor0
