\f1 ) fits this reading. Choice portions would be distributed by lot; this meat is so corrupted that lots are meaningless - just get it all out.\
But then verse 11's heating of the empty pot to cleanse the bronze suggests the corruption has spread to or been revealed in the vessel. Perhaps both are true sequentially: the contents were corrupted (bloody meat), the corruption spread to or was revealed in the pot, and by the time the contents are removed, the pot itself needs extreme measures.\
This might mirror the relationship between the people (contents) and the city/institution (pot). The people's bloodshed corrupted not just themselves but the place that held them. Even if you could remove the people, the city itself has become unfit.\
