\cf2 The hope isn't separate from the judgment but embedded in the same character of YHWH. The God who profanes the sanctuary is the God who will fill a new temple with His glory. The God who takes the delight of eyes is the God who will restore. The word that brings death is the word that will bring life to dry bones.\
And the path from here to there runs through the conditions chapter 24 creates: unmourned loss, rotting in iniquity, the knowledge of guilt that opens toward confession. The chapter ends the first section of the book not with resolution but with openness - to what YHWH will speak when the mouth opens, to what becomes possible when everything false has been stripped away.
