\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 The prohibition on mourning prevents processing loss as innocent suffering:
\b0  They cannot mourn normally because they are rotting in their iniquities. This keeps the wound open - they must sit in awareness of their own guilt, which is precisely the condition from which confession can emerge. The unmourned loss creates conditions for what comes next.\
\ls17\ilvl0
