\b0  Chapter 11's proverb - "this city is the pot and we are the meat" (meaning: we're the choice portions, protected) - is taken up and inverted. They are indeed the meat: corrupted meat with blood still in it, unfit to eat, not worth gambling for, removed piece by piece without distinction. The 
