\b0  Ezekiel's wife is 
\f2 \uc0\u1502 \u1463 \u1495 \u1456 \u1502 \u1463 \u1491 
\f1  
\f2 \uc0\u1506 \u1461 \u1497 \u1504 \u1462 \u1497 \u1498 \u1464 
\f1  - "the delight of your eyes." The sanctuary is 
\f2 \uc0\u1502 \u1463 \u1495 \u1456 \u1502 \u1463 \u1491 
\f1  
\f2 \uc0\u1506 \u1461 \u1497 \u1504 \u1461 \u1497 \u1499 \u1462 \u1501 
\f1  - "the delight of your eyes." YHWH takes from Ezekiel what YHWH Himself is giving up. The prophet bears in his body what YHWH is doing to His people. The sign isn't distant demonstration but participation in the loss.\
\ls17\ilvl0
\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	7.	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 The opened mouth marks structural transition:
\b0  Chapter 24 ends the first section of Ezekiel. The mouth that was closed (chapter 3) - restricted from reproof because they wouldn't hear - will be opened when the news comes (24:27, fulfilled in 33:22). The iron wall comes down. What wasn't possible before becomes possible when everything false has been stripped away.\
\ls17\ilvl0
\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	8.	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 The chapter creates conditions rather than just announcing outcomes:
\b0  The word accomplishes what it declares. The path is made real by the word. The unmourned loss, the rotting in iniquity, the stripped-away security - these are conditions for confession, for YHWH remembering covenant, for what Ezekiel will speak when his mouth opens.\
